1
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:03,000
Belê temaşevanên hêja,
 
Yes dear viewers,

2
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:06,000
vê carê jî me berê xwe da nav koçeran.
 
this time we directed ourselves to the nomads.

3
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Du gund in, gundê Gulîka û gundê Gobekê.
 
Two villages, Gulîka village and Gobekê village.

4
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:13,000
Ev her gund ji, di quntara Çiyayê Hawarê da hatine avakirin.
 
Both of these villages were built at the foothills of Mount
Hawar.

5
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:33,000
De ka em bihevra derbaz bin, em bihevra herdu gundan nas
bikin.
 
Let's pass together, let's get to know both villages
together.

6
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Merheba ji we ra.
 
Hello to you.

7
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

8
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Em we nas bikin destpêkê?
 
Can we get to know you first?

9
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:08,000
Navê min Îbrahîm e,
 
My name is Ibrahim,

10
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,000
lawê Mehmedê Îbrahîm im.
 
I am the son of Mehmed Ibrahim.

11
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
Ez ji gundê Gulîka me.
 
I am from the village of Gulika.

12
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Ser çava.
 
Upon my eyes (Welcome).

13
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,000
Sax bî.
 
Stay healthy.

14
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:14,000
Em te jî nas bikin?
 
Let us get to know you too?

15
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
Navê min Mihemed e,
 
My name is Mihemed,

16
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,000
ez ji gundê Gobekê me heval, lawê Selman im ez.
 
I am from the village of Gobeke friend, I am the son of
Selman.

17
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Ser çava.
 
Upon my eyes (Welcome).

18
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:21,000
Sax bî, ehlen we sehlen ser çava heval.
 
Stay healthy, welcome, upon my eyes friend.

19
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:24,000
Gundê Gulîka, gundê Gobekê.
 
The village of Gulika, the village of Gobeke.

20
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Niha em ê dîroka her gundekî bipirsin.
 
Now we will ask about the history of each village.

21
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Em ê destpêkê ji cem Îbrahîm destpê bikin.
 
We will first start with Ibrahim.

22
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

23
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Te got tu ji Gulîka yî.
 
You said you are from Gulika.

24
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Im.
 
Yes.

25
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Ev nav, ji ku hatiye, çi wateyê dide, çi me'neyê dide?
 
Where did this name come from, what does it mean?

26
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Ev navê Gulîka, fexdê me Gulîkî ye.
 
This name of Gulika, our clan is Guliki.

27
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Eşîra me Milî ye, fexdê me Gulîkî ye.
 
Our tribe is Mili, our clan is Guliki.

28
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Dibêjin berê da ê pêşiyê me gihiştine, xeberek dane,
 
They say in the past our ancestors arrived, they gave a
word,

29
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
dînan, nav lê dane Gulîka.
 
crazy ones, they named it Gulika.

30
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Ji wir da ji me re ma Gulîka, fexdê me Gulîkî ye heta niha.
 
Since then it remained Gulika to us, our clan is Guliki
until now.

31
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:51,000
Û tu Milî ye.
 
And you are Mili.

32
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Em Milî ne, eşîra me Milî ye.
 
We are Mili, our tribe is Mili.

33
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Piranî eşîra we li ku derê dikeve?
 
Where is the majority of your tribe located?

34
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Eşîra me li Bakur pir e.
 
Our tribe is plenty in the North (Turkey).

35
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Û li pêş Cizîrê jî pir e. Eşîra me mezin e, eşîreke mila
mezin e. Pir in.
 
And in the Cizire region it's also plenty. Our tribe is big,
it's a big branch tribe. They are plenty.

36
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Ê Gulîka çiqas mal e?
 
How many houses is Gulika?

37
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Gulîka dor heftê malî ye.
 
Gulika is around seventy houses.

38
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Û em gişt malbatek in, ji dê û bavekî ne.
 
And we are all one family, we are from one mother and
father.

39
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:17,000
Hûnaha kêm bîne di sê-çar malên nas dibin.
 
Maybe a few are less, in three-four houses they are known.

40
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:23,000
Vêra dibêjin Mala Mistîkêne, Me'mikêne, Silêmanikêne, Mala
Betel,
 
They call them the House of Mistiken, Memiken, Silemaniken,
House of Betel,

41
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,000
û Mala Ehmedê Silêmên, pênc-şeş merî ye me ne,
 
and the House of Ehmede Silemen, it is five-six people of
ours,

42
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:30,000
em gişt jî meriyên hev û pismamên hev in.
 
we are all relatives of each other and cousins of each
other.

43
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Hûn koçer in ne?
 
You are nomads right?

44
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Em gî koçer in berê, û em koçer in jî esesê me koçer e.
 
We were all nomads in the past, and we are nomads, our
essence is nomadic.

45
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:39,000
Te got koçerê Gulîkî em belavbûyî ne, gundên nêzîk in û
meriyên we li gundan pir hene?
 
You said we the nomads of Guliki are scattered, are they
close villages and do you have many relatives in the
villages?

46
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:42,000
Meriyên me li Sêmalka hene.
 
We have relatives in Semalka.

47
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Vêr dibêjin Mala Hemîdê Hemoçê.
 
Here they call it the House of Hemide Hemoce.

48
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Meriyên me li gundê Emo hene, vêr dibêjin Mala Şihînê
Gulîkî.
 
We have relatives in Emo village, here they call it the
House of Shihine Guliki.

49
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Meriyên me li Şiyê hene dibêjin Mala Osmanê Koçer.
 
We have relatives in Shiye, they call it the House of Osmane
Kocer.

50
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Û li van gundan gî hene û li gundên din jî hene.
 
And in these villages there are all of them and in other
villages too.

51
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Meriyên me li gîya hene.
 
We have relatives everywhere.

52
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Û hûn hemî jî xwedî pez in ne?
 
And you are all sheep owners right?

53
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Hemî xwedî pez in û ticar in.
 
Everyone is a sheep owner and traders.

54
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Û karê me pez e yanî. Koçer e, esasê xwe, kar û xebata xwe
pez e, karê me pez e.
 
And our job is sheep, I mean. Nomads, their essence, their
job and work is sheep, our work is sheep.

55
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,000
Tu jî ji Gobekê yî?
 
Are you also from Gobeke?

56
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Ez Gobekî me heval, erê.
 
I am from Gobeke friend, yes.

57
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:09,000
Ê Gobek çiqas mal e?
 
And how many houses is Gobek?

58
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:13,000
Weleh heval Gobek ta pa deh-panzdeh-şeş mal e.
 
By God friend, Gobek is maybe ten-fifteen-sixteen houses.

59
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:18,000
Em... em li vir heval sê-çar eyl in ha.
 
We... we are here friend three-four tribes here.

60
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Yanî hemî ji yek dê û bavekî ne?
 
Meaning they are all from one mother and father?

61
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Haho welleh heval... yanî em meriyê hev in hemû.
 
Oh by God friend... I mean we are all relatives of each
other.

62
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
Gobek, Gulîka em gî meruvê hev in.
 
Gobek, Gulika, we are all relatives of each other.

63
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
Me jin dane hev, em ji hev du zewicîne.
 
We gave women to each other, we married from each other.

64
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Em gî ji cem hev jinan distînin, em gî cem hev in.
 
We all take women from each other, we are all with each
other.

65
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Bi rastî dema berê derbazî gundê we dibûm,
 
Honestly, when I passed by your village in the past,

66
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,000
yani Gulîka û Gobekê min ra digotin ku tu cuda nîne.
 
meaning Gulika and Gobeke, they used to tell me that you are
not separate.

67
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
Em yek in heval. Em gundê Gobekê û Gulîka yek in.
 
We are one friend. We the village of Gobeke and Gulika are
one.

68
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Heta Şêxler, cem heval gî Efrîn, hin li vir a dor me hene...
 
Up to Sexler, by friend all of Afrin, there are some here
around us...

69
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Yanî em gî meriyên hev in heval.
 
I mean we are all relatives of each other friend.

70
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Em koçer li vir gî yek in hemû. Em gî ji gundekî ne, gundê
me yek e.
 
We nomads here are all one. We are all from one village, our
village is one.

71
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:54,000
Niha di Herêma Efrînê da çend gund koçer hene?
 
Now in the Afrin Region how many nomadic villages are there?

72
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:56,000
Weleh heval koçer pir in hemû.
 
By God friend the nomads are plenty all of them.

73
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Hinek li vir gundê derdorê Şiyê hene. Hinek li Sêmalkayê
hene.
 
Some are here in the surrounding villages of Shiye. Some are
in Semalka.

74
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Ê pir çûne Efrînê. Hinek çûne Helebê heval.
 
Most went to Afrin. Some went to Aleppo friend.

75
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:06,000
Ji ber me'îşet çetîn bû li vir gund hicre kirin, çûne der a,
bo me'îşetê çûne der a.
 
Because making a living was hard here they migrated from the
village, they went outside, for a living they went outside.

76
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Ê em mane em em ber xwedî pez mane.
 
And we who stayed, we stayed as sheep owners.

77
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Em ji... hinek... em in uste liqî dikin, ez in uste me. Em
li her... em kar dikin munan em dikin.
 
We also... some... we prune branches, I am a pruner. We do
everything... we do jobs we do.

78
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Ê ev e gundê me heval işt e...
 
And this is our village friend like this...

79
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:21,000
Ê em deh-panzdeh-şeş mal dikişin em di gund da mane, ê din
gî çûne der va.
 
And we ten-fifteen-sixteen houses draw we stayed in the
village, the others all went outside.

80
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Nexwe wek niha Îbrahîm axivîn kir hemî xwedî pez in, Gulîka.
 
Then as Ibrahim spoke now they are all sheep owners, Gulika.

81
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:27,000
Hûn ji xwedî pez in hemî?
 
Are you also all sheep owners?

82
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Em jî hemû xwedî pez in heval. Pezê me hene li vir a.
 
We are also all sheep owners friend. Our sheep are here.

83
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Em gîha... em gî xwedî pez in li vir a.
 
We all... we are all sheep owners here.

84
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Û em ser pez de'işin û zeytûnê me hene.
 
And we live off sheep and we have olives.

85
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Em milkî gîha ne em ser de'işin. Û li vir a ji heye.
 
We all have property we live off. And there is here too.

86
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Berê pêş da gel l vir dima, Gobek da l vir a...
 
Before in the past people stayed here, Gobek in here...

87
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:44,000
Ev da çûne çiya komir anedikirin.
 
Those who went to the mountains used to bring coal.

88
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Hin da pezê xwa hebî, hin da dewarê xwa hebûyî,
 
Some had their sheep, some had their cattle,

89
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
Da diçûn çiya da dihatin.
 
They used to go to the mountains and come.

90
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Ê naho işt e nema, komir nema, dewurê cût nema.
 
And now like this there isn't any, coal isn't there, plowing
cattle isn't there.

91
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Bes pez maye, û zeytûn mane em pê de'işin... hemû.
 
Only sheep remained, and olives remained we live off... all
of them.

92
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:57,000
Meriyên we hinek ji aliyê serxetê ji hene, aliyê Tirkiyê da?
 
Your relatives are some from the border side too, Turkey
side?

93
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:58,000
Hene heval, meriyên me hene.
 
There are friend, we have relatives.

94
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,000
Kîjan gundan a?
 
Which villages?

95
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Gobek e heval ewê ku ew çiya e
 
It's Gobek friend the one that is that mountain

96
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:05,000
dibên Gobeka malê Şêxim ê tekoçê dersin
 
they say the Gobek of Sexim's house...

97
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
a Şêx Seîdê bavê kur e Elî Riza
 
the one of Sheikh Said the father of the son Eli Riza

98
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:12,000
Li wir in. Û li Îslahiyê jî hene, merî yê me ê li wir ji
hene.
 
They are there. And in Islahiye too there are, our relatives
are there too.

99
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Û da bişikîn... niha gel hemî milet bişikî der a.
 
And they scattered... now people all nations scattered
outside.

100
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
Koçer li her derîkê bişikîne.
 
Nomads in every place are scattered.

101
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
Em ê hinekî ji ji Îbrahîm bipirsin,
 
We will ask a bit from Ibrahim too,

102
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Îbrahîm li hinekî li aliyê xetê da merivê we hene?
 
Ibrahim do you have relatives a bit on the border side?

103
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:30,000
Meriyên me hene û li Îslahiyê Gulîkan a naviyê gundî ji
Gulîka ye.
 
We have relatives and in Islahiye the Gulikans the name of
the village is Gulika too.

104
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Wir ji Gulîka ye. Te go Gulîkê Turkiyê û Gulîkê Sûriyê ev a
em gih merîyên hev in e.
 
There is also Gulika. You said the Gulika of Turkey and the
Gulika of Syria this is we are all relatives of each other.

105
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:39,000
Em gî pismamê hev din e û em gî meriyê hev din e.
 
We are all cousins of each other and we are all relatives of
each other.

106
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Wek başqe we debara xwe... hûn we bixwe bi çi dikin...
 
Like besides that your living... you yourselves what do you
do...

107
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
Zeytûn e ne...
 
Olives...

108
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Û dexl mexl e em diçînin, her weha em debarê mala xwe ew pez
e.
 
And grains we harvest, also we make a living for our house
those sheep.

109
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Û ekserî xwe gunda Gulîka em ticar in, ticarî ye...
 
And mostly ourselves the village of Gulika we are traders,
it's trading...

110
00:06:53,000 --> 00:07:00,000
Ekserî xwe ticareta pez dikin.
 
Mostly we do sheep trading.

111
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,000
Em carek din ji ji Hacî bipirsin.
 
Let's ask Haci once more.

112
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Haci naha av kehne li ba we hene li vir o?
 
Haci now do you have old springs with you here?

113
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:07,000
Weleh heval ji me re av a kehne li vir tin e l'gund,
 
By God friend for us an old spring is not here in the
village,

114
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,000
li vir ceme hafiyek me jor heyi ziyarek heye
 
here with us a bit up there is a shrine

115
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
dar e , tê da e avkî oveyê heye
 
there is a tree, inside it there is some water

116
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:15,000
jar dikeve wir a diben nav leikirine Fadel.
 
that falls there they named it Fadel.

117
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Nav lê kirine Fêdil.
 
Named it Fedil.

118
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Bera jî heval dema baran nedibariya, salê mihel vekê, salê
mihel,
 
Also in the past friend when rain didn't fall, a year of
drought like, a year of drought,

119
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:24,000
gelê berê em ê li vir sersalê dikir. Nav gund Gobek û Gulîka
em yek bûn,
 
the people of the past we used to do the new year here. In
the village Gobek and Gulika we were one,

120
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
me da hev ra sersalê kir heval.
 
we used to do the new year together friend.

121
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:28,000
Me da çû bi ber dewarê xwe cêrj e dikir, me da bi mirîşka
cêrjek dikir,
 
We used to go in front of our cattle doing rituals, we used
to do rituals with chickens,

122
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:32,000
Û bi xwedê jin em ê bibîn, baran da ser de lê dikir,
 
And by God women we would see, rain would pour down on us,

123
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:34,000
ava li wir da hişk nedibû.
 
the water there wouldn't dry up.

124
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Ava vir ew e.
 
The water here is that.

125
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Ziyaret heval... şehîdê hene...
 
The shrine friend... martyrs are there...

126
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Şehîd in heval... bes işt e... şûynek ji dûr didilê wir a,
dûrdilek hey...
 
They are martyrs friend... just like this... a place from
far that is there, a distance is there...

127
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Û e... dê ew e jî ava vir bîrekê heye... dibên Bîra Ebrozê.
 
And uh... that is also water here a well is there... they
say the Well of Ebroze.

128
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:47,000
Me diçû ava li vir nate ma, me diçû Ebroz ... avê li vir êdî
hişk nabe ye...
 
We used to go the water didn't stay here, we went to
Ebroz... the water here doesn't dry up anymore...

129
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Sala da demetiyayî... wele çû ber ava xwa jor da ber, ava
jor tinne da
 
The year that was a drought... by God went to their water up
there, the water up there wasn't there

130
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:53,000
û gûlik li vir a biya werdê gût Gûl o Bîda
 
and Gulik here came said Gul and Bida

131
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,000
me av ji wir da anîyê didan.
 
we brought water from there and gave.

132
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,000
Me diçû ji cem av e anîyê didan
 
We went from the water brought and gave

133
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
êdî niha ji bîreker a tên didan.
 
and now from the wells they bring and give.

134
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
ber ê av a me ya şikdar tine bî...
 
before our doubtful water wasn't there...

135
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
Ê naho... te behsa ew î... fêdil kir.
 
And now... you mentioned that... Fedil.

136
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Hê.
 
Yes.

137
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
Ê berî vê bi çend sala hûn diçûn war a?
 
And before this by how many years did you go to the camp?

138
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:10,000
Wella heval... beri vê... weke... heta noko pez li vir tê
avdan...
 
By God friend... before this... like... until now sheep are
watered here...

139
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
pez... heta noko... pez li vir tê avdan... pezê gund.
 
sheep... until now... sheep are watered here... the sheep of
the village.

140
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:14,000
i yek pezê xwe heya dera li vir... ta noko av dê...
 
one has his sheep up to there here... until now there is
water...

141
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,000
beri vê bi 20 sale yanî milet diçû wir de av tine av dê...
 
before this by 20 years meaning people went there and gave
water...

142
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
Diçûn sersalê wer a?
 
They went for the new year there?

