e.. û nûnî me wez jîmal dihât ..
 
Well, the shepherds among themselves, among the villagers,
every four shepherds give to each other, so the sheep become
many and we take them out. Then they graze closely together,
the sheep become like donkeys, leaving some droppings
behind, looking at the crop... predicting this... yes
friend... we made this round near... and bread also came
from home...

261
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Har roja non hedat?
 
Did the bread stay for days?

262
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:33,000
Har roja non em jî şev ê bi xwa de dihatin pirki meh ba da
nîra paşê bi dûtûro û min diçûn re ev pez min e derd. Eme
jber pez da em de çere em .
 
Every day we ate bread with milk at night, we milked it in
the morning and evening, then with a churn and I went out
with my sheep. We were looking after the sheep, grazing
them.

263
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:38,000
Nê xêçkî we dor sa mêrî xadan eva mêri xadan meha e e e?
 
Now, isn't there something around the master about this
master?

264
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Wevê çûke meh paşî da peze em de grin, em e ez debkên nate
da em ez denibê navin bêhî el cerê em ez tûwre arte e de ser
e fiken
 
Oh little one, the month after the sheep we will catch, we
will do it... we will fall among the sheep...

265
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Daviya me?
 
Our end?

266
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:59,000
Daviya mi e daki mi dazi mî we ewe berxi tê ne, em e we xêj
bişanê. Em ji me wekî diçin birê xwe.
 
My end... my mother... my father... they bring the lambs, we
will graze them with our sheep. We go to our flock like
them.

267
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:01,000
Jikukve dev di şêre he?
 
Does the mouth open from the throat?

268
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:21,000
Jikukwa ev derîye de mêrgî çuçuk kin, û emê şîşo kên şişik
ji vê şîrê bidin pênçkê zûrokê em ve dikin de va çîkê tiji
şîr be ki weh ha wekî ve baxikê.. xos narî çê alemê neri ..
pişk pîra kin ez derîcem e
 
From the throat to the little meadow, and we will skewer it,
give it milk from this milk, pinch the belly we open in the
udder full of milk like this, like this belly... nobody
looks at anyone else... the old sheep, I am talking about
her...

269
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Barê bi tenê.. bêri bê tenê?
 
Before it was alone... milk alone?

270
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:32,000
Parê bi tanê sa ba xêz bê no amlê dihelî xê.
 
Last year alone, like a single sheep, no hope in dissolving
itself.

271
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:35,000
E e tû e pazi te bi re e?
 
Is your sheep coming?

272
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Eme tû we cûzane peye xoji me kir hî.
 
Our sheep are coming to graze in our yard.

273
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:46,000
E e tû e şixûl e pîçuk e ez qeri xoji me?
 
The job is small, I'm satisfied with my sheep?

274
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:52,000
Awe de piçike me parî ji nav me fer me farwê, ewe ferwe e
 
Oh little one, the sheep is among us, we milk it, it's a
milker...

275
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Piştî xwarinê derxistin, paşê şer xist?
 
After feeding, you take it out, then bring it back?

276
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:10,000
Parê min derketê ji cama ji wê, pişte wî min naxwazî. Piştî
te min naxwazî pêçike min.. pêra kin na wê tîre bîker hî
hiye ez re,
 
After it leaves the glass, from that, after that I don't
want it. After you, I don't want it my little one.. after
that it will be milked, I tell you,

277
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Tên de bi tirkî na e navê wî?
 
It doesn't have a Turkish name?

278
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Nawînê xê pi xane di kete ma jî min de em e me re ax bi xîna
baxce xe... no rûn diçe ma me re. Em me le qaçim farûvye wa
fer ve tê ha rodve ta be xet.
 
It doesn't have a name... we call it reading in the
garden... its butter goes with us. We wear our shoes and go,
let's read it, let it be on the line.

279
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:31,000
Ewe fêrwe ew deriye de her redi devirde der kêtê?
 
Does this reader always read and extract outside?

280
00:18:31,000 --> 00:18:42,000
Qanî de mi wexta na xaze, qanî pîri wê ji cem wî de e xwe di
de biskine, aw ji min tîye e pe min nawze xelas qedya .
 
Sometimes when it doesn't want, when it is old, it sits from
it, it stops itself, he from me thirst... I don't want to
finish it.

281
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:45,000
E pîşt wê zuwda tu...
 
And after that, you...

282
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:50,000
Şa xwarê pîştê min nexwaze nav pêşê ... temî la cama çavîne
..
 
After eating... after it doesn't want in front... wait near
the eyes...

283
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:53,000
Tu milcana di çavîne?
 
Do you look at the face?

284
00:18:53,000 --> 00:19:01,000
Çawana pazi her hî ro derv naxwîn da ron xwîn ni min ri
reşem ne... mirye la cama ne... ev jî me we ne...
 
Like sheep, everyday taking out to eat... until I eat I am
not satisfied... the sheep near me are not... this is also
our...

285
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:06,000
Dêngî gêngiye? Dêngî naxwazî dîka min naxwzê.. ji ker xal me
xala wê?
 
The sound is echoing? The sound doesn't want, my heart
doesn't want... from our uncle's donkey?

286
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Ji keve avderiye ji mêrê denga e... we min şixulî ji ve pîne
re . xal sêr keti.. .
 
From where it falls in the yard, from the voice... we worked
for this job... the uncle's secret fell...

287
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Xwe me almin na. Çima xe a sa de bal min in .
 
They don't know themselves. Why are they with me.

288
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Nê melba de me ye be ci çi be . Xebate de na ve be.. . Speza
ware ...Xalas xala... Spas abdrahman...
 
Look in the house we are... whatever it is. No more work...
Good morning... Thanks uncle... Thanks abdulrahman...

289
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:47,000
Salê du caran mihan û berxên xwe diqusinin. Û heriya ji bo
bazarganiya difiroşin. An ji xwere gundî dikin balîf û
doşek.
 
They shear their sheep and lambs twice a year. And they sell
the wool for trade. Or the villagers make pillows and
mattresses for themselves.

290
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:53,000
Digel vê gundî karê çandiniyê jî dikin û di serî de darên
zeytûnê cih digre.
 
Besides this, the villagers also do agriculture, primarily
olive trees.

291
00:19:53,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Digel çandiniya dexlû zeviyan, ceh, genim û colban.
Pehdebûna...
 
Along with the cultivation of cereals, barley, wheat, and
vetch. The emergence...

292
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:09,000
Mal li gund hiştiye ko aramiyan hiştibûne di gundê xwe da
bimînin, û rên pêşiyan ko çêkiribûne wê ra girtin.
 
The families left in the village, whom the peace allowed to
stay in their village, adopted the ways of the ancestors
that they had created.

293
00:20:09,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Ziyaretgeha Fadil li jor li aliyê bakur dikeve.
 
The Fadil shrine is located above, on the northern side.

294
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:17,000
Tê da av heye û ava wê tîcarî kêm nabe.
 
There is water in it, and its water never decreases.

295
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:22,000
Xelkê gund diçin wir, ji bo barîna baranê li ber Xwedê
digerin.
 
The village people go there and pray to God for rain.

296
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:26,000
Belkî bi ya wan bike û dilê wan bi barîna baranê şa bike.
 
Perhaps He will fulfill their wish and gladden their hearts
with rain.

297
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:29,000
Li aliyê rojava geliyê kûr heye.
 
On the western side, there is a deep valley.

298
00:20:29,000 --> 00:20:37,000
Ku ji gundê Şêx Kîlê dest pê dike û ta deşta Kitxê diçe.
 
Which starts from the village of Sheikh Kile and goes up to
the Kitx plain.

299
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:42,000
Li pêşiya herdu gundan û ji aliyê başûr va deşta Avrazê ye.
 
In front of both villages, on the southern side, is the
Avraz plain.

300
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Hemû bîdarên zeytûnê ne. Li başûr bîreke avê bi navê bîra
Avrazê heye.
 
They are all olive orchards. In the south, there is a water
well called the Avraz well.

301
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Û ta naha ava wê heye. Di demên berê da gundiyan bi dewaran
ava wê dikişandin.
 
And it still has water. In the past, the villagers used
animals to draw its water.

302
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:59,000
Li bakur rojava û li ser çiyayê Hawarê keleha Hawarê dikeve.
 
In the northwest, on the Hawar mountain, lies the Hawar
castle.

303
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:16,000
Û dîroka wê gelekî kevnare. Ta dîroka Horiyan diçe.
 
And its history is very ancient. It goes back to the history
of the Hurrians.

304
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:21,000
Wekî jina koçer, karê te yê berê çi bû?
 
As a nomad woman, what was your past work?

305
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Ê de wele, koçeriya berê da em diçûn, em bi pez dibûn.
 
Well, in the past nomadism, we used to go, we used to tend
to the sheep.

306
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Me şivantî bi xweser dikir.
 
We did the shepherding ourselves.

307
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:30,000
Û ji pey ra me ciyê pezê xwe pak dikir.
 
And then we cleaned our sheep's place.

308
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:34,000
Û ji pey ra me tiştê gundê xwe tevdikir. Em diçûn şîrê xwe,
me şîrê xwe didot.
 
And then we prepared our things in the village. We went to
our milk, we milked it.

309
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:37,000
Me didot, me dihat, me dikir penêr.
 
We milked, we came back, we made cheese.

310
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Me dida hev, em dikişandin vir, me dikir penêr.
 
We collected it, brought it here, we made cheese.

311
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:44,000
Me ji penêr şûnda, me mastê xwe yê ko dima digirt.
 
After the cheese, we made yogurt from what was left.

312
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:49,000
Me ji wê şûnda, me gijê dikir. Yanê mast, penêr, şîr.
 
After that, we made dairy products. Meaning yogurt, cheese,
milk.

313
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
Em dibêjin firû, lor, lûrik, gijê ye.
 
We call them firû, lor, lûrik, that is dairy.

314
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:54,000
Me gijê dikir.
 
We made dairy.

315
00:21:54,000 --> 00:22:00,000
E naha carna wekî ku çêdibin sîrik, we sîrik çêdikirin?
 
And now, sometimes they make sîrik (garlic cheese), did you
make sîrik?

316
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:03,000
Em ê kelandî radikin.
 
We keep the boiled one.

317
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:04,000
Yanî sîrik li ba we tine ye?
 
So you don't have sîrik?

318
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:07,000
Na. Em ê kelandî radikin.
 
No. We keep the boiled one.

319
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:13,000
Em ji ê şûnda dikin tûr, ji ê şûnda dikin şeqêne, an wekî
penêr...
 
After that we put it in a sack, after that we put it in a
skin bag, or like cheese...

320
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:16,000
Em didin ber rojê. Em dikin gulêlîk.
 
We put it in the sun. We make it into small balls.

321
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:18,000
Em berdidin nav zeytê.
 
We put it into oil.

322
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:22,000
Û em penêrê xwe yê kelandî başqe ye. Ê badayî başqe ye.
 
And our boiled cheese is different. The twisted one is
different.

323
00:22:22,000 --> 00:22:28,000
Ê firû başqe ye. Ê mast yê ko dima başqe ye.
 
The firû is different. The remaining yogurt is different.

324
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Girtî her tiştek başqe ye.
 
Overall, everything is different.

325
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:34,000
Ê da heywanê we ku çêdibin hûn derên beriyê?
 
Mother, when your animals were born, did you go to the
plains?

326
00:22:34,000 --> 00:22:37,000
Ê wele, ji payîzê da şûnda em derên. Pez li mal be em narin.
 
Well, after autumn we go out. If the sheep are at home, we
don't go.

327
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:39,000
Ev tiştan bi destê xwe çêkirine?
 
Did you make these things with your own hands?

328
00:22:39,000 --> 00:22:41,000
Bi destê xwe, gelî tiştî kes nedidan me.
 
With my own hands, no one gave us anything.

329
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:46,000
Ev no... ev no hev jî, mecmu'a ne.
 
These ones... these ones are from the collection.

330
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:49,000
Hê, bi destê xwe.
 
Yes, with my own hands.

331
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:52,000
Ev o...
 
This one...

332
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,000
Ev o destxetekî on a.
 
This is a handwoven one.

333
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:57,000
Te bi kî re çêkiriye?
 
Who did you make it with?

334
00:22:57,000 --> 00:23:00,000
A va min lawkê xwe re çêkiriye. Ê qîzkan min daye yê.
 
I made this one for my son. I gave the girls' ones to them.

335
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
Ev no yê lawkê min in a.
 
These ones are my son's.

336
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
Yanî te ji mêj va çêkirine evana?
 
So you made these a long time ago?

337
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Ev o du sal sê sal in, ez êdî çê nakim.
 
It's been two or three years, I don't make them anymore.

338
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:09,000
Êdî çavê min ji ber hev derketin, min dev ji berda. Çê
nakim.
 
My eyes have given out on me, I stopped. I don't make them.

339
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:17,000
Biner.
 
Look.

340
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:19,000
Te qîzkên xwe jî elimandin evana?
 
Did you teach your daughters these too?

341
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:20,000
Me elimandin e.
 
We taught them.

342
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:26,000
Qîzkên min tentene, qenewîc, ha va dor û berê xwe usa gişkî
bi destê xwe çêkirine.
 
My daughters made lace, cross-stitch, and all the things
around them with their own hands.

343
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:31,000
Gişkî. Gişkî destê xwe ye.
 
All of it. All of it is their handiwork.

344
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:35,000
Baş e xaltîcan, em herin cem dayikê jî. Dayê merhaba, çawa
yî te ra?
 
Okay auntie, let's go to mother too. Hello mother, how are
you?

345
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,000
Baş im.
 
I'm good.

346
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:37,000
Ev cilat te çêkir?
 
Did you make these clothes?

347
00:23:37,000 --> 00:23:40,000
Ev o me hêra rîst. Hêra.
 
We spun this wool. Wool.

348
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:46,000
Û me ziya kir, me bi efşiyan dî nê pêşiya xwe, me geş kinî.
 
And we stretched it, we carded it, we combed it out.

349
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:50,000
Me hazir kir, û me bi teşiyê rîst. Bi teşiyê, dest...
 
We prepared it, and we spun it with a spindle. With a
spindle, hand...

350
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:55,000
Û me gişk rîst, me bada, me ber bi hirfiyê da boyax kir.
 
And we spun it all, we twisted it, we gave it to the artisan
to dye.

351
00:23:55,000 --> 00:24:00,000
Me anî, teva kir û gezî... me çêkir, me bada, me şand gundek
dî.
 
We brought it, put it in the loom and measured it... we made
it, we twisted it, we sent it to another village.

352
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:05,000
Gundek cî... ew dest bi tevnan kir, û em naha pa da ev ho
çêkir.
 
Another village... he started the looming, and now we made
this like this.

353
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:12,000
Di ortê me da, me dirût. Û ev rişin o me bi xwe badan.
 
We sewed it in the middle. And these fringes, we twisted
them ourselves.

354
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:20,000
Me ta şeb xwes rîst, û bada, û bi wê şûnda, pezî me hebû, em
diçûn şivaniyê me diçûn...
 
We spun the threads beautifully ourselves, and twisted them,
and after that, we had sheep, we went shepherding, we
went...

355
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:29,000
Me pezî xwe didot. Me şîrê xwe dikir talme, me nanê xwe
dikir, ez diçûm êzinga, ez diçûm avê.
 
We milked our sheep. We put our milk into buckets, we made
our bread, I went for firewood, I went for water.

356
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:31,000
Dayê hûn ji kîjan gundî ne?
 
Mother, which village are you from?

357
00:24:31,000 --> 00:24:35,000
Em nêzîkî wî gundî ne. Ez ji Erebo me. Em li vî gundî mehr
kirîn.
 
We are near this village. I am from Erebo. We were married
in this village.

358
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:37,000
Te ji gundê Erebo ha mer kiriye?
 
You got married from the village of Erebo to here?

359
00:24:37,000 --> 00:24:38,000
Erê, min li vî gundî mêr kirî.
 
Yes, I got married in this village.

360
00:24:38,000 --> 00:24:40,000
Çend sal e tu vî gundî yî?
 
How many years have you been in this village?

361
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Ez nizanim çend sal in diqet. Qîçkê min mezin bûn... gişta
qîçkê xwe zawicandine, de mêr dane me.
 
I don't know how many years exactly. My children grew up...
they all married off their own children, and gave us men.

362
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:50,000
Te qîz da Erebo jî, we?
 
Did you give a daughter to Erebo too, or what?

363
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:51,000
As e min da...
 
I gave...

364
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:54,000
Dayê kê cil çêdikirin di gund da? Başqa te kî hebû?
 
Mother, who made clothes in the village? Who else was there
besides you?

365
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:56,000
Hese hebû...
 
There was Hese...

366
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:57,000
Di gund de... te û kê va cil çêdikirin?
 
In the village... who did you make clothes with?

367
00:24:57,000 --> 00:25:11,000
Me bi hev re dikir. Ez û pîrekek jî diyê kurê we ya hana, û
gurmê min, û jinek ji cîrana, me bi hev re dikir.
 
We did it together. Me and a woman, your son's mother there,
and my daughter-in-law, and a woman from the neighbors, we
did it together.

368
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:17,000
Me bi hev re dirîst, me bi hev re boyax dikir, me bi hev re
rîst, me bi hev re çêdikirin.
 
We spun together, we dyed together, we spun together, we
made them together.

369
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:21,000
Me di çûnê êzinga, em bi hev re diçûnê avê. Me bi hev re
penêr çêdikir.
 
We went for firewood together, we went for water together.
We made cheese together.

370
00:25:21,000 --> 00:25:27,000
Me bulxur dikişand. Me bulxur dikota. Me dihêrî. Me dikir
çolê xwe.
 
We ground bulgur. We pounded bulgur. We ground it. We took
it to our fields.

371
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:31,000
Qey te behsek xweş çêkir hebû ne. Keşkula me bida yekê...
 
You made a nice story, it was like this. If only you could
give us a bowl of it...

372
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,000
Heb e.
 
There is.

373
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:33,000
Heb e.
 
There is.

374
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:34,000
Hê.
 
Yes.

375
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:46,000
Ev tişt heye. Aha ev, aha ev. Tiştên weha, me bi hev re weha
dikir... weha dikir, weha dikir. Em weha çê dikin. Em bi
destê xwe didin hev.
 
This thing exists. Look here, look here. These things, we
used to do it together like this... like this, like this. We
make it like this. We gather it with our hands.

376
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:48,000
Ev jî hêrî ye.
 
This is also wool.

377
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:54,000
Û bazirkan ha weha, zarokên çûka... em li ser orxan girê
didin.
 
And these cords like this, for the small children... we tie
them on the quilts.

378
00:25:54,000 --> 00:25:55,000
Xalê tu dikarî carekî rîs bikî?
 
Auntie, can you spin thread once?

379
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:57,000
Na me sê sê çêkirin.
 
No, we made it in threes.

380
00:25:57,000 --> 00:25:58,000
Ê bi kîjan anî?
 
How did you bring it?

381
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:01,000
Ê de min ev da yê... lawkê xwe, yek da... min yek jê xira
kir, yek da...
 
Well, I gave this to my son, gave one... I ruined one of
them, gave one...

382
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:03,000
Xalê ev kî çêkiriyê? Xweliya vira ya?
 
Auntie, who made this? The ashes from here?

383
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:06,000
Ew bavê te çêkiriye.
 
Your father made that.

384
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:09,000
Ha ew rahmetî bo ya!
 
Oh, the late one made it for you!

385
00:26:09,000 --> 00:26:17,000
Û me pê re, ji wan ra dî dida. Û me di vira da hêrî çêdikir,
me tîna, dikir.
 
And we used to give them dye with it. And we used to make
wool here, bring it, and do it.

386
00:26:17,000 --> 00:26:19,000
Dayê hemî te çêkirin evana?
 
Mother, did you make all of these?

387
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:21,000
Hê bavo, hekîb e. Ew hekîba gûhî ye.
 
Yes my son, it's a hekîb (saddlebag). That's a side
saddlebag.

388
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:24,000
Kî stiriya? Te stiriya bi destê xwe?
 
Who sewed it? Did you sew it with your own hands?

389
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:33,000
Û wexta diçûn destê pêşî, destpê kirin... û ev hekîbê xist
nava da... hekîbê tiştên wek buxçê dikirin wî hekîbî.
 
And when they first went, they started... and put this
saddlebag inside... they put bundle-like things in this
saddlebag.

390
00:26:33,000 --> 00:26:38,000
Û gava siwar dibin bar kir. Wexta ku min bar kir siwariyê,
hespekî girto... hespekî reş...
 
And when they rode, they loaded it. When I loaded it on the
rider, took a horse... a black horse...

391
00:26:38,000 --> 00:26:45,000
Ev dî hekîbek e wî alî da buxçek da dî. Quncê hekîb jî daye
dest bûkê... wê gavê tiştên xwe bar kirin di ser da. Sandoqê
bûkê bûn.
 
This other is a saddlebag on that side, with another bundle
in it. The corner of the saddlebag was given to the bride's
hand... then they loaded their things on top. They were the
bride's chests.

392
00:26:45,000 --> 00:26:54,000
Sandoq dudu bûn, du sandoqên tije... xalîceyek bû, ev caw
bûn, nêrîn bûn... qamçî hekîbek wek tiştî wî de bûn.
 
There were two chests, two full chests... there was a rug,
there were these cloths, there were goat hair rugs... the
whip was like something else inside.

393
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Yanî qamçî bûkê bi destê xwe... bi destê xwe dikirin?
 
Meaning the bride's whip with her own hand... she made it
with her own hand?

394
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:01,000
Qamçî bûkê bi destê bûkê de bû wek wê çaxê.
 
The bride's whip was in the bride's hand at that time.

395
00:27:01,000 --> 00:27:04,000
Yanî qet nedidan xortan ha?
 
So they didn't give it to the young men, huh?

396
00:27:04,000 --> 00:27:13,000
Ê me cîz bûn, em keç bûn em biçûk bûn, em diçûn ew hono
kirina me dî...
 
Well, we were girls, we were young, we used to go and see
that doing...

397
00:27:13,000 --> 00:27:25,000
Gundê Gobekê gelekî kevnar e û dîroka wî ta dirêjahiya çar
sed salî diçe.
 
The village of Gobek is very ancient, and its history goes
back up to four hundred years.

398
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:33,000
Gelek kes ji xelkên gund berê xwe dane bajarê Efrîn, Heleb û
Şamê. Û li derveyî welat niştecih bûne.
 
Many people from the village have headed to the cities of
Afrin, Aleppo, and Damascus. And they have settled abroad.

399
00:27:33,000 --> 00:27:35,000
Lewma gund fireh nebûye.
 
Therefore, the village hasn't expanded.

400
00:27:35,000 --> 00:27:38,000
Bîst û pênc xanî di gund de hene.
 
There are twenty-five houses in the village.

401
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:41,000
Û nêzîkî dused kes li gund jiyan dikin.
 
And about two hundred people live in the village.

402
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:45,000
Lê gelek kes li derveyî gund jî jiyan dikin.
 
But many people also live outside the village.

403
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:51,000
Gundê Gobekê bi pirbûna şikeftan navdar e. Û nêzîkî deh
şikeft lê hene.
 
The village of Gobek is famous for its abundance of caves.
And there are about ten caves there.

404
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:58,000
Di demên berê da ew şikeft wekî xanî dihatin bikaranîn û
gundiyan tê da jiyan dikir.
 
In the past, those caves were used as houses and the
villagers lived in them.

405
00:27:58,000 --> 00:28:12,000
Her weha wekî cihê sewalan û... embarxane jî bi kar dihatin.
 
Also, they were used as places for animals and... as storage
rooms.

406
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:15,000
Ê qesê te kirin, qîzê ra te kirin?
 
Well, did they talk about you, did they ask for the girl?

407
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:19,000
Ê wa, du textirê barî ew e.
 
Yes, there are two layers of loads, that's it.

408
00:28:19,000 --> 00:28:21,000
Ka niha bes ji me ra qala karê xwe yê berê bike.
 
Come on now, just tell us about your past work.

409
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:26,000
Ê karê berê me çi kar dîtin, kar giran bû.
 
Well, what past work did we see, the work was heavy.

410
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:30,000
Me kar dikir, bar giran bû... bi dar da.
 
We worked, the load was heavy... on wood.

411
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:31,000
Te çi kar dikir?
 
What work did you do?

412
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Me gelek kar dikir, me dew didot, mast çêdikir...
 
We did a lot of work, we milked for ayran, made yogurt...

413
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:41,000
Mast çêdikira... cîh da dianî... em mastê dikira ta
dixwara...
 
Made yogurt... brought it to the place... we made yogurt for
you to eat...

414
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:47,000
Di derdiketa holê te bixwara...
 
It would come out so you could eat...

415
00:28:47,000 --> 00:28:50,000
Me li gund wisa dikir... me bi xwe kar dikir.
 
We did it like this in the village... we did the work
ourselves.

416
00:28:50,000 --> 00:28:54,000
Çend sal ez weha me... pazdeh sal em weha bûn... wey Xwedê!
 
How many years I was like this... fifteen years we were like
this... oh my God!

417
00:28:54,000 --> 00:29:00,000
Heta ko kar diqediya... em bi xebatê re bûn...
 
Until the work was finished... we were with the labor...

418
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:05,000
Ê ka te çawan ew kar dikirin, wilo giran bû te kar dikir?
 
And how did you do that work, was it that heavy for you to
work?

419
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:07,000
Ez dakevim... ez bar hilgirim...
 
I go down... I lift the load...

420
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:08,000
Tu diçû ciya?
 
You used to go places?

421
00:29:08,000 --> 00:29:12,000
Erê, me diçûm cih an...
 
Yes, we used to go to places...

422
00:29:12,000 --> 00:29:18,000
Ez radibûm ez dakevim şikefta dakevim... ta nîvro dimam...
min pez dîtin e.
 
I would get up, I would go down to the cave... stay until
noon... I watched the sheep.

423
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:27,000
Pênc sal me şivantî kir, me gund dîtin... pênc sal me pez
xwedî kirin li gund!
 
For five years we shepherded, we watched the village... for
five years we kept sheep in the village!

424
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:34,000
Û me hema xwedî dikirin da em bixwin... em xwebixwe kar
dikin. Xwedê!
 
And we just kept them so we could eat... we work ourselves.
My God!

425
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:39,000
Xalê te qet tiştek bi destê xwe çêkiriye mîna cilan, tiştan?
Çend sal te çêkiriye evana?
 
Auntie, have you ever made anything with your own hands like
clothes, things? How many years did you make these?

426
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:44,000
Me pêra... me hirî şûşt, hirî... û me rîstiya...
 
Together... we washed wool, wool... and we spun...

427
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:52,000
Heta panzdeh, çardeh saliya me, me çêdikira...
 
Up until we were fifteen, fourteen years old, we made it...

428
00:29:52,000 --> 00:29:56,000
Qenc te bîr aniye... kî kar dikir bi te re?
 
You remembered well... who worked with you?

429
00:29:56,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Me yek bi yek di gund da bi qîzan re kar dikir... heya em
derdikevin.
 
We worked one by one in the village with the girls... until
we came out.

430
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:04,000
Ê kesî, başqey te karê dî nake l'vir da?
 
Does anyone else besides you do any other work here?

431
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:08,000
Nizanom dikirin, zor dikirin.
 
I don't know, they used to, they used to do a lot.

432
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:11,000
Da niha nakirin, hokî milêt da hemî gij dikin cem in o.
 
But now they don't, now the people all gather together.

433
00:30:11,000 --> 00:30:14,000
Ê do gundik ko, hin hatine nav ro.
 
And these two villages, some have mingled together.

434
00:30:14,000 --> 00:30:16,000
Ê Avrozê, hin hatine nav ro.
 
Some from Avrozê have mingled.

435
00:30:16,000 --> 00:30:18,000
Ê Şexkêlê, yek yek nav ro.
 
From Şexkêlê, one by one among them.

436
00:30:18,000 --> 00:30:20,000
Bav gundî Mi'emê, hin din nav ro.
 
The village of Mi'emê, some others are among them.

437
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:22,000
Ê Gubakê gişt li kuye?
 
Where is everyone from Gubakê?

438
00:30:22,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Ez diçim cem.
 
I go to them.

439
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:28,000
Na te vî demî te textir tinne bî?
 
Were there no doctors back then?

440
00:30:28,000 --> 00:30:31,000
Tinne bî.
 
There were none.

441
00:30:31,000 --> 00:30:36,000
Paşê textir derketin o, misteşfê derketin o.
 
Later doctors appeared, hospitals appeared.

442
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:43,000
Filon derketin o, ew derketin o.
 
Such and such appeared, those appeared.

443
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:45,000
Pê me dibirin cem a wî.
 
Then we used to take them to him.

444
00:30:45,000 --> 00:30:47,000
A vê rê re diçûm.
 
I used to go down this road.

445
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:50,000
Çendik a vê ro çûne.
 
Several have gone this way.

446
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:53,000
Aw hebû a... navê xwa Fikret bî.
 
There was one... her name was Fikret.

447
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:55,000
Em bi vê ro diçûn cem.
 
We used to go to her on this road.

448
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:58,000
Wê hewa ava bî, ni derket...
 
Her home prospered, now she left...

449
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:05,000
Me dibirin diçûn mixser.
 
We took them and went to the hospitals.

450
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:08,000
Na tu çend salî ye?
 
So how old are you?

451
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:14,000
Welleh, ez nizanim. Birakî min dibê ji giştî hefteyê de...
 
By God, I don't know. My brother says from the whole
seventy...

452
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:18,000
Bîst û, heşt û, yek û, didin e, ez nizanim.
 
Twenty, eighty, one, two... I don't know.

453
00:31:18,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Birakî min wiha dibêje ho.
 
My brother says like this.

454
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:23,000
Birakî min... di salan ji min çûktir e.
 
My brother... is two years younger than me.

455
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:24,000
Birakê te heye ji?
 
You have a brother too?

456
00:31:24,000 --> 00:31:25,000
Erê welle, birak ji... xweş e.
 
Yes by God, my brother... he's good.

457
00:31:25,000 --> 00:31:31,000
Di salan ji min çûktir e.
 
He is two years younger than me.

458
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:34,000
Î wî heştê bê e... î min heştê û sê ne.
 
If he is eighty... I am eighty-three.

459
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:38,000
Gî wî heştê e... î min heştê ne.
 
If he is eighty... I am eighty.

460
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:41,000
Ez nizanim, ho nişte... we gi dina xwendin...
 
I don't know, it's like this... Like reading...

461
00:31:41,000 --> 00:31:44,000
Aha de hey... qeyde me xwendin e, me kî dî xwendin e?
 
Look... where did we have schooling, where did we read?

462
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:49,000
Em ûmî ne. Titişkî nizanin.
 
We are illiterate. We don't know anything.

463
00:31:49,000 --> 00:31:50,000
Xweş gundê Avrozê ye?
 
Is the village of Avrozê nice?

464
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:51,000
Xweş e ji Avrozê re arê.
 
It is nice for Avrozê, yes.

465
00:31:51,000 --> 00:31:53,000
Tê bi kû ve gundî ye?
 
Where are you originally from?

466
00:31:53,000 --> 00:31:57,000
Dê hatim l'vir o.
 
I came here.

467
00:31:57,000 --> 00:32:01,000
Ez hatim vê derê... Erê.
 
I came to this place... Yes.

468
00:32:01,000 --> 00:32:08,000
Ê dayê çi tê bîra te, dema berê tu keçik bû, te hate vî
gundî, ev gunda berê çawa bû? Ev gunda hole ne bû? Mezin bû?
 
Mother, what do you remember, when you were a girl and came
to this village, how was this village before? Was this
village not like this? Was it big?

469
00:32:08,000 --> 00:32:12,000
Gund ji vir firehtir bû.
 
The village was larger than this.

470
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:14,000
Da gundî Mi'emê dî ye, a gundî han o.
 
Then that village of Mi'emê, that village there.

471
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:16,000
Gî hatin vir in, e.
 
They all came here.

472
00:32:16,000 --> 00:32:18,000
Gî hatin vî gundî ne, gî yê derdorê çûn e.
 
They all came to this village, everyone around left.

473
00:32:18,000 --> 00:32:21,000
Wexta ku ji wê re xirfîne ne, ne nizanim.
 
When it comes to that, since I got old, I don't know.

474
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:24,000
Lî, Gubakê kê maye ey?
 
But, in Gubakê who is left, eh?

475
00:32:24,000 --> 00:32:28,000
Ê berê... a berê ev gunda çawa bî? Berê we li wir çi kar
dikirin gunda?
 
And before... how was this village before? What work did you
do in the village before?

476
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:30,000
Ne çi kar dikirin?
 
What work did they do?

477
00:32:30,000 --> 00:32:35,000
Dema havîn dibû, em diçûn pale, diçûn zeytûna...
 
In the summer time, we used to go harvesting, go to the
olives...

478
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:38,000
Em diçûn rizin o, qeşko diçirand...
 
We used to go to the vineyards, prune the branches...

479
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:41,000
Karê me hev bû. Karê me dikir hev in.
 
This was our work. The work we did was this.

480
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:44,000
Xwendin tine... Filan tine... Bêvan tine...
 
No education... No this... No that...

481
00:32:44,000 --> 00:32:47,000
Em tiştekî nizanin.
 
We don't know anything.

482
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:53,000
Lî, karê me berê dikir ev in.
 
But, the work we used to do before was this.

483
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:55,000
Mala te ava be, siheta te xweş.
 
May your house prosper, health to you.

484
00:32:55,000 --> 00:33:00,000
Ya we jî xweş... Xwedê ji we razî be...
 
Yours too... God bless you...

485
00:33:00,000 --> 00:33:14,000
Beriya di nava gundê Gubekê de kaniyek avê hebû.
 
Before, in the village of Gubekê, there was a water spring.

486
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:17,000
Û xelkê gund ava vexwarinê jê peyda dikirin.
 
And the village people obtained their drinking water from
it.

487
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:20,000
Lê naha ava wê miçiqî ye.
 
But now its water has dried up.

488
00:33:20,000 --> 00:33:22,000
Her du gundên Gulîka û Gubekê...
 
The two villages of Gulîka and Gubekê...

489
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Xwedî têkiliyek baş û hevkariyek xurt in.
 
Have a good relationship and strong cooperation.

490
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:34,000
Weke yek gund jiyan dikin û tevdigerin.
 
They live and act like one village.

491
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:35,000
Merheba ciwano.
 
Hello young men.

492
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:36,000
Ehlen û sehlen.
 
Welcome.

493
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:37,000
Çawa yî? Te baş e?
 
How are you? Are you well?

494
00:33:37,000 --> 00:33:38,000
Baş im sipas, tu çawa yî. Baş î, rind î tu?
 
I am fine, thanks, how are you? Are you well, are you fine?

495
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:40,000
Xwedê te bihêle, rebbî.
 
May God keep you, Lord.

496
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:41,000
Silav te.
 
Greetings to you.

497
00:33:41,000 --> 00:33:44,000
Siheta we xweş. Ka em bi te carek nas bikin e.
 
Health to you. Let us get to know you for a moment.

498
00:33:44,000 --> 00:33:47,000
Hene ji Gubekê ne, hene ji Gulîkan e...
 
Some are from Gubekê, some are from Gulîkan...

499
00:33:47,000 --> 00:33:55,000
Çîrokas xweş e, jiyanek navbera hev da, du gund gihiştine
hev di, û wana gi jiyanek tê da hene, hemî jî xwediyê pez in
e.
 
Their story is nice, a life among each other, two villages
joined together, and they all have a life in them, and all
of them are owners of sheep.

500
00:33:55,000 --> 00:34:00,000
Ê naha di gund de çend xanî hene? Naha di nav baxsa xwe
anî...
 
Now how many houses are there in the village? Now speaking
of your own...

501
00:34:00,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Di gund de, dudu xanî ne.
 
In the village, there are two houses.

502
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:08,000
Em dêr kavrikê nêr dixirin e, em xizmetê dikin ê.
 
We go and buy ram lambs, and we provide care for them.

503
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:12,000
Yanî yê zeîf em dixirin, em xwedî dikin.
 
That is, the thin ones we buy, we raise them.

504
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:16,000
Mesela me ji ereban dianîn genim, ceh, baqil, ka... ev tişt
yanî em didin e.
 
For example, we used to bring from Arabs wheat, barley,
broad beans, straw... these things, I mean, we give them.

505
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:20,000
Weznê wan giran dibe... yanî rind dibî, qelew dibî, em dibin
e.
 
When they gain weight... I mean, they get good, they get
fattened, we take them.

506
00:34:20,000 --> 00:34:26,000
Çûka da difiroşin. Û ew xwa dellal in, dellal e pez di
kantonê Efrînê da.
 
To the market we sell them. And he himself is a broker, a
sheep broker in the Afrin canton.

507
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:28,000
E dellal im jê...
 
I am a broker too...

508
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,000
Ê xudaniyê xaniyê kî ne?
 
And who are the owners of the houses?

509
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:32,000
Xudaniyê... xaniyê... ez im... û ew jî birayê min e. Nêl vir
e.
 
The owners... of the houses... it's me... and that one is my
brother. He's not here.

510
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:38,000
Ne l'vir e, ew çûne pez bikirin aw. Û Elî va. Elî jî pisnamê
me ye.
 
He's not here, he went to buy sheep. And Ali here. Ali is
also our cousin.

511
00:34:38,000 --> 00:34:43,000
Yanî ew jî xwediyê pez... çûne pez, ew jî di nav gunda qorê
dixirin, î peziyan in e.
 
I mean he is also an owner of sheep... they went for sheep,
they are also in the village buying flocks, they deal with
sheep.

512
00:34:43,000 --> 00:34:45,000
Hûn berxwa dikirin, pez dikirin?
 
Do you buy lambs, do you buy sheep?

513
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:49,000
Em berxwa ji dixirin, em mihan jî dixirin, em bizinan jî
dixirin... yanî çêbe, em gi dixirin e.
 
We buy lambs too, we buy sheep too, we buy goats too...
whatever is there, we buy it all.

514
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:52,000
Û bes ev xaniyê da em xizmetê dikin ê.
 
And only in these houses we provide care.

515
00:34:52,000 --> 00:34:54,000
Berxik nêr em pir qelew dikin.
 
We mostly fatten male lambs.

516
00:34:54,000 --> 00:35:02,000
Û qesabê mentiqê Efrîn... gişt tên cem me, yanî ew xaniyê
pez berxwe dixirin, yê dibin şerjê dikin.
 
And the butchers of the Afrin region... they all come to us,
I mean those sheep houses buy lambs, take them and slaughter
them.

517
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:03,000
Hemî l'vir in?
 
Are they all here?

518
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:05,000
Erê hemî pir giş cem me ne.
 
Yes all, this many are at our place.

519
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:07,000
Wî we noçerî naxwîn an şivan hene ji we re?
 
Do you not graze them or do you have shepherds for them?

520
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:10,000
Ne, berxê nêr em noçerî nin. Berxê nêr tim da di xaniyê da
am xizmetê dikin e.
 
No, the male lambs we don't graze. Male lambs always inside
the house we provide care for them.

521
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:22,000
Yanî diştan em cihê... nexale a genim... şile gişt nav hev
dixin û şixilê me ji hêna... ji marra xizmetê dikin ê.
 
I mean things like barley... bran... wheat... grains all
mixed together and our workers here for us... provide care
for us.

522
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:25,000
Û qelew dikin em difiroşin.
 
And we fatten them and we sell them.

523
00:35:25,000 --> 00:35:27,000
Yanî meişeta me, ser vî tiştî ye.
 
I mean our livelihood is on this thing.

524
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:28,000
Te got ez dellal im a?
 
You said you are a broker?

525
00:35:28,000 --> 00:35:29,000
Em dellal im, a.
 
I am a broker, yes.

526
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:31,000
Û hûn dudu ye, ticar e.
 
And you two, are merchants.

527
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:36,000
Ez û birakê, Evdilqadir em herdu muşerekê dikin e.
 
Me and that brother, Evdilqadir, we both do partnership
together.

528
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:38,000
L'vê ro alîkarên hev in.
 
Here you are helpers of each other.

529
00:35:38,000 --> 00:35:43,000
Ez birayê çûcik, em ticar in. Em hatine cem birayê Qadir em
kê dewêr bikin ji xwa re pez...
 
I am the small brother, we are merchants. We came to brother
Qadir so we can do a rotation for ourselves with sheep...

530
00:35:43,000 --> 00:35:44,000
Na hûn tevî hev kar dikin?
 
Now do you work together?

531
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:51,000
E hen dellal e, henek şivan e, hene gi ticar in, evna nav da
erê...
 
Yes some are brokers, some are shepherds, some are
merchants, among each other these yes...

532
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:53,000
Û na... tu hatî bikirî ye?
 
And now... you came to buy?

533
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:55,000
Erê ez hatim bikirim, erê.
 
Yes I came to buy, yes.

534
00:35:55,000 --> 00:35:56,000
Na tu hatî çî bikirrî?
 
Now what did you come to buy?

535
00:35:56,000 --> 00:36:00,000
Ez hatime mihan a berxan, çi lê hat em dikirin.
 
I came for sheep or lambs, whatever is available we buy.

536
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:03,000
Eger wextê ku hatin ev pez nakirin.
 
If they come and don't buy these sheep.

537
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:10,000
Ê ev pezê nêr sekine... ew kî hatin ya bi kîlo dikirin, ya
serniga dikirin.
 
And these male sheep are waiting... whoever came will either
buy by kilo, or buy by head.

538
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:14,000
Li gorî alekê dexin û didin... delal jî mafê xwe... delal
e... ew buxane.
 
Depending on the situation they offer and give... the broker
also gets his right... the broker... he will take.

539
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:16,000
Xwe nava peze çawa ye?
 
How is it among the sheep?

540
00:36:16,000 --> 00:36:18,000
Em ne pê ve ye ne jî.
 
We don't step away from it.

541
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:23,000
Bes texmînce em dizanin çend kîlo ne... yanî ya dudu kîlo
kêmin... ya dudu zêde ne, hawa.
 
But by estimate we know how many kilos they are... I mean
either two kilos less... or two kilos more, like that.

542
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:30,000
Naha tişkî din te bipirsim... naha sûkê Efrînê sêşem e...
hûn dirin wê bazarê?
 
Now let me ask you something else... now Afrin market is on
Tuesday... do you go to that market?

543
00:36:30,000 --> 00:36:38,000
Em dirin bazarê... Em bi xwe dellalin, em dirin bazarê sêşem
e, û bazarê Raco. Em bin ê xwa ri dên, em milletê kurd da...
rî xwa di cam ê gird di dê.
 
We go to the market... We ourselves are brokers, we go to
the Tuesday market, and Raco market. We take our things, we
Kurdish people... gather around them.

544
00:36:38,000 --> 00:36:44,000
Artix em ji yê de froş in ê. Yanî xwediyê pez nî firoşe e
ye. Em ji de froşin e.
 
Then we sell it from there. I mean the owner of the sheep
doesn't sell it. We sell it from there.

545
00:36:44,000 --> 00:36:49,000
Kî ye ji cem wa difroşa... em jam wa difroşe...
 
Whoever from them sells... we sell from them...

546
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Ê çi qas e heqê seriyekê te?
 
And how much is your fee for one head?

547
00:36:51,000 --> 00:37:01,000
Delaliyê xwe? Sed warqa... em sed warqa dibin. Her yek em
difiroşin de sed werqa em didin.
 
His brokerage? A hundred notes... we take a hundred notes.
Each one we sell we give a hundred notes.

548
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:10,000
Nebelkî difiroşê... defrek ro wî heye pêncî difroşe... sedî
firoşe... hesabê piyaser e.
 
Maybe he sells... ten for him... sells fifty... sells a
hundred... it depends on the market.

549
00:37:10,000 --> 00:37:19,000
Elvirrind pê pez rind dare. Elver tu nabe sor bî. Yane hesab
de ew... hey bîsto difroşe, aw heye pêncî difroşe bazar e...
dewê re ev e.
 
Over here sheep go well. Over here it doesn't happen that
it's cold. I mean it depends... you have someone selling
twenty, you have someone selling fifty at the market... the
cycle is this.

550
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:27,000
Naha em paqî bikin, ka we çawa bikin a... tu yê bîfiroşî ewi
dellale.
 
Now let's see, look how you do it... you will sell, he is
the broker.

551
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:31,000
Ez naha... az daxwaz dikim ji te...
 
I now... I request from you...

552
00:37:31,000 --> 00:37:34,000
Ez dellal im... naxwa as kî difroşime.
 
I am the broker... otherwise I will sell it.

553
00:37:34,000 --> 00:37:36,000
Naha az... ez dellal im.
 
Now I... I am a broker.

554
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:43,000
Ez dellal im, ez kî bifroşim e.
 
I am a broker, I will sell it.

555
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:49,000
Naha tu pir giran e... sihra pezan nizanin... em bi nê xwa
sûkê dîn.
 
Now you are too expensive... they don't know the market for
sheep... we go and see our market.

556
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:58,000
Em bêjin sed hezar... tu te de bidî bîst warqa te didin...
 
Let's say a hundred thousand... you will give twenty notes
they give...

557
00:37:58,000 --> 00:38:10,000
Û dellal e didin o, we daxin...
 
And the broker they give, they discount...

558
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:21,000
Ez dellal im, di cem te daxwazim a difiroşim o, ji cem yek
din daxwazim a difiroşim... ez de nav xelkê difiroşim.
 
I am a broker, I request from you and sell, and from someone
else I request and sell... I sell among people.

559
00:38:21,000 --> 00:38:29,000
Niha ez yekî bikirim... we yê difiroşim wê naha...
 
Now if I buy one... he will sell it now...

560
00:38:29,000 --> 00:38:30,000
Qe te ra ne behs ke...
 
Never negotiate with you...

561
00:38:30,000 --> 00:38:44,000
Û bira te... dellal o... me li cem camêran...
 
And your brother... broker... we are with gentlemen...

562
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:51,000
Bes em bi xwe nizanin baha wê, ne kîloyan nizanin ev yeka...
 
But we ourselves don't know its price, nor do we know the
kilos of this one...

563
00:38:51,000 --> 00:39:00,000
Di nav şar re ji yek ji ha he, evna re firoş me, ez kîloyek
bi firoşim...
 
In the city too there is someone like this, we sell these to
them, I sell a kilo...

564
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:04,000
Niha ez hatim yek bikirim, ev ka, tu yê bi çendî bidî min?
 
Now I came to buy one, this one here, how much will you give
it to me?

565
00:39:04,000 --> 00:39:12,000
Naha yek ev hat a wera bi min razî... te got tu dê bidî min
bi çendî...
 
Now one came here with my consent... you said you will give
it to me for how much...

566
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:20,000
Welle bi şiklek am baha naxeş bikin... baha yê rinde e, e w
de buhin...
 
By God, in a way we make the price nice... the good price
is, that we take...

567
00:39:20,000 --> 00:39:27,000
Em bînin dellal e, baha yê de e... em didin e.
 
We bring the broker, the price of... we give.

568
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:30,000
Na ev çendî? Çend hezar kî?
 
Now how much is this? How many thousands?

569
00:39:30,000 --> 00:39:34,000
Ew ev ne, yê şûna ne... ev bîst û pênc hezar...
 
This one here, the one over there... this is twenty-five
thousand...

570
00:39:34,000 --> 00:39:37,000
Î he bîst û sê difiroşin, hawa.
 
There are those they sell for twenty-three, like that.

571
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:44,000
Niha me got ez dellale wiya, ka we çawa dellale wiya bixaze
k çewê defroşin e?
 
Now we said I am his broker, look how will you ask for his
brokerage, how will you sell it?

572
00:39:44,000 --> 00:39:51,000
A wî dellal e, ez difiroşim e... az de te de firoş...
 
He is a broker, I will sell... I will to you sell...

573
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:52,000
Na tu daxwaz bike.
 
Now you request.

574
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:58,000
Te daxwaz kir ye, ez defroşime.
 
You requested one, I sell it.

575
00:39:58,000 --> 00:40:00,000
Naha ew bîst û sê ye.
 
Now it is twenty-three.

576
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:00,000
Lê wuda, lê wuda? Temam, temam de kerem ke de. Em herin.
 
No I five... I sell...

577
00:40:00,000 --> 00:40:02,000
Lê wuda, lê wuda? Temam, temam de kerem ke de. Em herin.
 
Over there, over there? Okay, okay, go ahead. Let's go.

578
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:03,000
Fermo.
 
Go ahead.

579
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:17,000
[Muzîk]
 
[Music]

580
00:40:17,000 --> 00:40:20,000
... Kîlo, kîlo, fiderê kîlo dixwinin.
 
... Kilo, kilo, they weigh by the kilo here.

581
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:21,000
Na em bazar dikan.
 
No, let's bargain.

582
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:22,000
Erê em bazar dikan.
 
Yes, let's bargain.

583
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:24,000
Heval vê derê noka kîlo bi çi didin?
 
Friend, how much do you sell a kilo of chickpeas for here?

584
00:40:24,000 --> 00:40:26,000
Kîlo bi hezar dused û pêncî wareqî.
 
A kilo is 1250 liras.

585
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:28,000
E... pere buhaye lê nayê bî çend bidin?
 
Eh... it is expensive, won't you give it for less?

586
00:40:28,000 --> 00:40:30,000
Na pirr e. He? Na pirr e.
 
No, it's a lot. Huh? No, it's a lot.

587
00:40:30,000 --> 00:40:32,000
Ê em çi bidin, ne we ne we, em çi bidin?
 
Eh, what should we give? Neither you nor us, what should we
give?

588
00:40:32,000 --> 00:40:34,000
Bi çi terzî dixwazî be, hezar sedî behs bike.
 
Whatever you want, let's talk about 1100.

589
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:36,000
Dused çawa? Hezar sedî behs bike.
 
How two hundred? Let's talk about 1100.

590
00:40:36,000 --> 00:40:38,000
Hezar dused û bîst û pênc waraqî te be birinîye...
 
1225 liras if you want to take it...

591
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:43,000
Ha... te go em kîşan bifroşin, kî hesabê we kirî... me
hesabê we te kirî...
 
Ha... you said how we'll sell, who calculated it... we did
your calculation...

592
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:46,000
Bi çi terzî be em bidin. Hezar sed û pêncî jê be.
 
However you want it, we'll give it. Take it for 1150.

593
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:47,000
Law te xwe re dusedî girtiye nayê xwarê?
 
Boy, you're stuck at two hundred, won't you come down?

594
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:49,000
Hezar û dused û bîst û pênc waraqa be.
 
Let it be 1225 liras.

595
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:50,000
Hezar û dused û bîst û pênc.
 
1225.

596
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:52,000
Law te we re dusedî girt, te xwe girt girt dused...
 
Boy, you are stuck at two hundred, you kept yourself at two
hundred...

597
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:57,000
Ji we re... em birayên hev in em aliyê hev in, hezar û dused
wekela xwedê be.
 
For you... we are brothers, we are from the same side, let
it be 1200 for God's sake.

598
00:40:57,000 --> 00:41:00,000
Ê me gelek kirî hezar dusedî. Te çi qebûl kirî?
 
Well, we bought a lot for 1200. What did you accept?

599
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:02,000
Kîlo bi hezar û dusedî ye.
 
A kilo is 1200.

600
00:41:02,000 --> 00:41:06,000
Ê bikişîne ser qapanê, yallah kîso bavêje ser qapanê.
 
Well, weigh it on the scale, come on put the bag on the
scale.

601
00:41:06,000 --> 00:41:07,000
Yallah ser qapanêkin.
 
Come on put it on the scale.

602
00:41:07,000 --> 00:41:11,000
[Muzîk]
 
[Music]

603
00:41:11,000 --> 00:41:18,000
Gundê Gulîka û Gobekê, gundên yekemînne ko bazirganiya
sewalan jê mih û bizinan dikin.
 
The villages of Gulîka and Gobekê are the first villages
that trade in sheep and goats.

604
00:41:18,000 --> 00:41:25,000
Lewma xelkên gund debar jiyana xwa bikirîn û firrotin û
herweha xwedîkirina sewalane.
 
Therefore, the villagers make a living by buying and selling
and also raising animals.

605
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:29,000
Û berhemên wan libazarrên Efrîn û navçeyan difroşin.
 
And they sell their products in the markets of Efrîn and the
districts.

606
00:41:29,000 --> 00:41:36,000
Sê xanên pez ligund hene, gotêda nêzîk sêsed mih û berx jibo
serjêkirinê têne xwedî kirin.
 
There are three sheepfolds in the village, where nearly
three hundred sheep and lambs are kept for slaughter.

607
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:43,000
Qesabên Efrîn û bajarokan têne jibo kirîna berxan û xwarina
goşt jivirr dikirrin.
 
Butchers from Efrîn and towns come to buy lambs and buy meat
for consumption from here.

608
00:41:43,000 --> 00:42:03,000
[Muzîk]
 
[Music]

609
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:38,000
Belê temaşavanên hêja, me bi hevre du gund naskirin, livirjî
emê xatirê xwe jiwe bixwazin.
 
Yes, dear viewers, we got to know two villages together, and
here we will say goodbye to you.

610
00:42:38,000 --> 00:42:43,000
Em gihîştine dawiya bernameya xwe. Heta hefteyekî dîn emê
dîsa bi hev re bin, bimînin di xweşiyê de.
 
We have reached the end of our program. Until next week we
will be together again, stay well.

611
00:42:43,000 --> 00:42:48,000
[Muzîk]
 
[Music]

